on\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d43e38c9d7bc4757d8804564309b893daf69b49ecc86003adb339433428afd22","event_uuid":"a7e8bc12-e523-4afa-8aa2-54d80f0ca042","position":{"commit_sha":"1c627f4bdc62050700c424ac66e372a09507000c","position":"1785808978502654001-a7e8bc12-e523-4afa-8aa2-54d80f0ca042"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"503e0f889153e825ca9fb421c61f0b4e2e2ae075bcc501acef0fb39a456aefe1","event_uuid":"cbdefa62-e997-4a9f-97c8-dc3e9ef7a510","position":{"commit_sha":"c4e269b97a02a95bdc64c4ed11b7c4856e6226d3","position":"1785809713416156001-cbdefa62-e997-4a9f-97c8-dc3e9ef7a510"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Corrected the provisional diagnosis before claim or host mutation after inspecting commits 4214516f95 and 31844d5f9f. The committed Click override and lock are correct and must be consumed, not weakened. The actual updater defect is its unlocked pipx VCS install, which bypasses the workspace-only override and requests the declared-incompatible eval+dev pair. Revised plan: exact-SHA versioned checkout, uv sync --locked with runtime/operator extras and --no-dev, locked Click/pip-audit proof, atomic publication, and launchd verification.","timestamp":1785808124289317001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fourth plan review PASS, blocking=0. Accepted the minor P6 advisory without another material edit: the remaining conjunctions each define one atomic observed state transition (log+exit and all-old/all-new tuple) and will be exercised by one probe. The one-time migration is covered by the three post-publication resolution ACs and will also be checked before kickstart. The implementation will stage current.new beside current and use one same-filesystem atomic replace, never ln -sf.","timestamp":1785808978502654001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation and verification complete. Preserved commit 4214516f95 lock canonicalization and commit 31844d5f9f Click override unchanged; repository pyproject.toml and uv.lock have no local diff. Replaced unlocked pipx resolution with exact git ls-remote SHA checkout plus uv sync --locked --no-dev and runtime/operator extras mcp, reviewbot, ui, agents, eval, tracing, grounding, grounding-t2. Final script SHA-256 is 97d02f757caa3972fed9e7faf2c2375011eeedd42df7b91e79d2f75e7ea46527; original preserved at evidence/.../rebar-dev-update.before.sh with SHA-256 cdf36f53da6f0a2b56438a90f68b7154a9c93b813ffa8fc350568a357e04b6ba. Disposable probe probe-updater.sh (SHA-256 b0aa46d1bd6ff6a8c2b1766ba4e2159560269c2af622e3e4e1ce16b1f36c83c3) passed sync rejection/log/current preservation, smoke rejection/log/current preservation, all-old before current rename, all-new after rename, exact locked extras, single-release retention, and post-publish crash retention healing. Real launchd run 246 exited 0 and published exact remote SHA 57c8d908a6c1ec67b47786429e9265033914ee10. current -> releases/57c8d908...60147; rebar, rebar-mcp, and last-good.sha all resolve through current into that release. Both help smokes pass. importlib reports Click 8.4.2 and rebar source under the exact-SHA release. uvx pip-audit over the published site-packages exited 0: No known vulnerabilities found (therefore no PYSEC-2026-2132). Global rebar review-plan --status loaded repository criteria and returned the expected stale-code status for this edited host dependency, not a configuration error. Process census found no reconcile-bridge, probe-rebar, or rebar bridge process. Immediate launchd run 247 exited 0 and logged no change (already on 57c8d908a6c1ec67b47786429e9265033914ee10). No repository code change or Gerrit review applies to this machine-local bug.","timestamp":1785809713416156001}],"created_at":1785807775929050001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"35f00528-ff89-4c3e-a074-d184e79c1dc0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3592-0d1e-2bd6-4e22"}],"description":"## Context\nThe hourly host updater `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` installs a Git URL through pipx. Commit `4214516f95` made the repository uv-lock-canonical and declared the `eval`+`dev` extra combination incompatible; commit `31844d5f9f` correctly overrides Inspect AI's stale `click<8.2.2` cap and locks Click 8.4.2 to remediate PYSEC-2026-2132. The override is workspace-only and is not published in wheel metadata. The updater therefore bypasses both the committed lock and the Click override, and its 2026-08-04 01:27 run failed unlocked resolution while leaving the global host runtime stale at `d72c4777`. This blocks A2-2 and later A6-1 rollout evidence.\n\n## Approach\n- Preserve `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, the Click override, and all dependency declarations unchanged.\n- Replace the pipx VCS-resolution step with an exact-SHA, versioned local checkout under the updater state directory and `uv sync --locked`.\n- Sync the runtime/operator extras `mcp`, `reviewbot`, `ui`, `agents`, `eval`, `tracing`, `grounding`, and `grounding-t2` with `--no-dev`. Development tools are intentionally excluded from the global runtime; `eval` remains available, and the declared `eval`+`dev` conflict is respected.\n- Retain the existing single-flight directory lock. Build and smoke-test an unpublished candidate. A rejected candidate logs `candidate <sha> rejected at <stage>`, exits nonzero, and leaves the current pointer untouched.\n- Make `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar`, `rebar-mcp`, and `last-good.sha` stable links through one updater-managed `current` symlink. Each release contains its `.venv` and a `sha` file. Publication stages `current.new` and atomically renames that one symlink to `current`; the two executables and checkpoint therefore switch at one filesystem commit point. One-time migration establishes the stable links before scheduled publication and verifies all three resolve through `current`.\n- After successful publication retain only the published release; remove rejected candidates and superseded releases so hourly updates cannot grow the state directory without bound.\n- Trigger the updater through launchd and verify an immediately following no-op.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The updater checks out the exact SHA returned by `git ls-remote`. Tier: deterministic script-content check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The updater runs `uv sync --locked` inside that exact-SHA checkout. Tier: deterministic script-content check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The sync requests `mcp`, `reviewbot`, `ui`, `agents`, `eval`, `tracing`, `grounding`, and `grounding-t2` with `--no-dev`. Tier: deterministic script-content check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The script change does not modify repository `pyproject.toml` or `uv.lock`. Tier: repository diff check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An injected sync failure logs `candidate <sha> rejected at sync` and exits nonzero. Tier: disposable-state failure probe.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An injected sync failure leaves `current` byte-identical. Tier: disposable-state failure probe.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An injected smoke failure logs `candidate <sha> rejected at smoke` and exits nonzero. Tier: disposable-state failure probe.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An injected smoke failure leaves `current` byte-identical. Tier: disposable-state failure probe.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Crash probes immediately before and after the `current` rename observe either all-old or all-new resolution for `rebar`, `rebar-mcp`, and `last-good.sha`, never a mixed tuple. Tier: disposable-state publish-boundary probe.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] After successful publication, only the published release directory remains under updater-managed releases. Tier: disposable-state success probe.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A launchd-triggered real install exits 0 and advances `last-good.sha` to the exact `origin/main` SHA used for the run.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar` resolves through `current` into the versioned exact-SHA runtime.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar-mcp` resolves through `current` into the same versioned exact-SHA runtime.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The published runtime reports Click 8.4.2.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `pip-audit` reports no PYSEC-2026-2132 finding for the published runtime.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The published global build loads this repository's effective criteria without a configuration error.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `rebar --help` exits 0 against the published runtime.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `rebar list --help` exits 0 against the published runtime.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] An immediately following launchd run logs `no change (already on <installed-sha>)` and exits 0.\n\n## Files\nMachine-local `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` and updater-managed state under `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/state/rebar-dev/`; no repository files.\n\nScope: S. Discovered while collecting A2-2 rollout evide